<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions six-month bonds in operation.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions six-month bonds in operation.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it auctioned short-term federal bonds worth 400 million rupees in a special open market operation on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said bids worth 2.65 billion rupees were submitted by banks, but bids worth only 400 million rupees were accepted for the outright sale of the six-month bonds at a maximum cut-off of 15 percent per annum.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
